ChangeLog for QtParted:
-----------------------
* 1.0.0 (2026-10-29)
  - Rewrite for Qt 6 (C++20, CMake); all Qt 3/Qt 4 and Qt/Embedded code removed
  - New GUI-independent core modelled on GParted 1.8.1: 64-bit sector
    arithmetic, libparted backend, libblkid probing, pending operation queue
    with visual preview, merging and undo, operations applied in a worker
    thread with a detailed, savable log
  - Create partition tables of every libparted type (gpt, msdos, ...)
  - Create primary/extended/logical partitions with MiB, cylinder or no
    alignment and a graphical resizer; delete; format; clear signatures
  - Partition flags and GPT partition names, queued as operations
  - 21 file systems with tool detection, size limits and usage reporting
  - Busy detection: mounts, active swap, device-mapper/LVM/MD holders
  - File System Support dialog, Partition Information dialog
  - pkexec launcher with polkit policy, X11/XWayland and Wayland support;
    desktop file and AppStream metadata
  - Disk image files can be opened from the command line
  - Resize and move partitions (primary, logical and extended) with a
    graphical editor; file systems are resized with their own tools or
    libparted (FAT, HFS), moved with an internal block copy that is rolled
    back on failure, NTFS boot sectors are updated, swap is recreated with
    its label and UUID; mounted file systems can be grown online
  - Copy and paste partitions into free space (optionally larger) or over
    an existing partition
  - Check and repair file systems, set file system labels, new UUIDs
  - File System Support dialog lists grow/shrink/move/copy/check/label/UUID
  - LUKS: open and close encryption with a passphrase kept in locked memory;
    resize open LUKS together with the file system inside, check, label,
    UUID, format and copy of its content; move and grow closed LUKS
  - Mount on fstab mount points, unmount, swapon/swapoff, LVM Volume Group
    activation, applied immediately like in GParted
  - Usage of reiserfs and reiser4; mounted ext2/3/4 report their full size
  - Italian translation; English plural forms; translations built into the
    program, new languages picked up from translations/*.ts
  - User manual (doc/manual) shown in Help > Contents (F1)
  - --help and --version work without a display
  - Packages: .deb with CPack, Arch PKGBUILD, Fedora spec; CI builds a .deb
  - Unit tests and end-to-end tests on image files and loop devices

* 0.6.0 (2012-04-07)
  - Support Parted >= 3.0
  - ext2, ext3, ext4, xfs, jfs, btrfs, FAT FS creation support
    without relying on parted filesystem code
  - Some (but still nowhere near enough) code cleanups
  - Improved UI for editing external tools

* 0.5.0 (2011-02-17)
  - Switch to Qt 4.x

* 0.4.x (never released, if you really need it grab it from SVN)
  - More code cleanups
  - Support parted >= 1.7.x

* 0.4.5 (2005-08-12)
  - Fix up "&" signs being displayed in the menus w/ Qt 3.3.4
  - Add workaround for parted bug showing CD-ROMs as partitioning targets
  - Some code cleanups
  - Some bugfixes

* 0.4.4 (2004-04-25)
  - Added hidden flags for FAT/NTFS filesystem
  - Added support for read label (Fran?ois Dupoux)
  - Added Catalan translation (Dani Hernandez)

* 0.4.3 (2004-03-13)
  - Improved stability with fs wrappers
  - New ntfsresize wrapper (tested with 1.8 and 1.9)

* 0.4.2 (2004-03-04)
  - Fixed compilation errors with Qt-3.3
